# Keep the build-time zh-Hant dictionary and its generator LF on every platform,
# so the drift guard (`scripts/gen-zh-hant.ts --check`, run by check-docs / the
# CI node job) compares byte-identical on Windows too. Without this, the default
# `core.autocrlf` on the Windows runner checks these committed LF files out as
# CRLF, and the guard reports spurious drift (green on macOS/Linux, red on
# Windows). The guard also normalizes EOL defensively; this pins the on-disk form.
*.generated.ts text eol=lf
scripts/gen-zh-hant.ts text eol=lf
